        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Sarah will use <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 90]</span> beads to make <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3]</span> identical necklaces. How many beads will each necklace have? </p>",
            "readable_text": "Sarah will use [MATH: 90] beads to make [MATH: 3] identical necklaces. How many beads will each necklace have?",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To determine the number of beads each necklace will have, we need to calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 90\\div 3.]</span></p><p>Remember that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 90]</span> in expanded form is</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9 \\times 10.]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 90 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|.]</span></p><p>Then, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 10|=; (9 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 10|=; 3 \u00d7 10|=; 30]</span></p><p>Therefore, each necklace will have <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 30]</span> beads.</p>",
            "readable_text": "To determine the number of beads each necklace will have, we need to calculate [MATH: 90\\div 3.]\n\nRemember that [MATH: 90] in expanded form is\n\n[MATH: 9 \\times 10.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 90 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 10|=; (9 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 10|=; 3 \u00d7 10|=; 30]\n\nTherefore, each necklace will have [MATH: 30] beads.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSarah will use [MATH: 90] beads to make [MATH: 3] identical necklaces. How many beads will each necklace have?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo determine the number of beads each necklace will have, we need to calculate [MATH: 90\\div 3.]\n\nRemember that [MATH: 90] in expanded form is\n\n[MATH: 9 \\times 10.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 90 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 9 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 3|=; 9 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 10|=; (9 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 10|=; 3 \u00d7 10|=; 30]\n\nTherefore, each necklace will have [MATH: 30] beads."
      },
