        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 280 \\div 7?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "What is [MATH: 280 \\div 7?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Remember that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 280]</span> is the same as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 28]</span> tens. So, we have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 280 = 28 \\times {10}.]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 280 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|.]</span></p><p>Then, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00f7 7 \u00d7 10|=; (28 \u00f7 7) \u00d7 10|=; 4 \u00d7 10|=; 40]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 280\\div 7 = 40.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Remember that [MATH: 280] is the same as [MATH: 28] tens. So, we have\n\n[MATH: 280 = 28 \\times {10}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 280 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00f7 7 \u00d7 10|=; (28 \u00f7 7) \u00d7 10|=; 4 \u00d7 10|=; 40]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 280\\div 7 = 40.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 280 \\div 7?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that [MATH: 280] is the same as [MATH: 28] tens. So, we have\n\n[MATH: 280 = 28 \\times {10}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 280 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 28 \u00d7 10 \u00f7 7|=; 28 \u00f7 7 \u00d7 10|=; (28 \u00f7 7) \u00d7 10|=; 4 \u00d7 10|=; 40]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 280\\div 7 = 40.]"
      },
