          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Remember that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3,200]</span> is the same as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 32]</span> hundreds. So, we have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3,200 = 32 \\times {100}.]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3, 200 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|.]</span></p><p>Then, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00f7 4 \u00d7 100|=; (32 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 100|=; 8 \u00d7 100|=; 800]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3,200\\div 4 = 800.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Remember that [MATH: 3,200] is the same as [MATH: 32] hundreds. So, we have\n\n[MATH: 3,200 = 32 \\times {100}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 3, 200 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00f7 4 \u00d7 100|=; (32 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 100|=; 8 \u00d7 100|=; 800]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 3,200\\div 4 = 800.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCompute the value of [MATH: 3,200 \\div 4.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that [MATH: 3,200] is the same as [MATH: 32] hundreds. So, we have\n\n[MATH: 3,200 = 32 \\times {100}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 3, 200 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|.]\n\nThen, we swap the order of the multiplication and division:\n\n[MATH: 32 \u00d7 100 \u00f7 4|=; 32 \u00f7 4 \u00d7 100|=; (32 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 100|=; 8 \u00d7 100|=; 800]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 3,200\\div 4 = 800.]"
